Check environment configuration

Verifies that your environment is properly configured for Antithesis testing. Runs health checks — container runtime, docker compose, the tenant and container registry settings, and your credentials (stored by snouty login, which the user runs in a terminal, or set in the ANTITHESIS_* environment variables). A missing registry is a warning, because only a launch needs it. To see the settings that snouty resolved, run `settings_show`.

The credential can be a sign-in or an API key from snouty login, an API key in ANTITHESIS_API_KEY, or a GitHub Actions OIDC token.

doctor also contacts the Antithesis API. It confirms that your credential works, reports the API and tenant versions, and warns when the tenant release is too old for a command. It also tells you when your tenant has an Antithesis registry that the registry setting does not use. Use `offline` to skip the checks that contact the API.

The command fails if any required check fails.

With `json`, the output is one JSON object, with the fields ok and checks. ok is false when any check has status error. checks is a list of checks, each with the fields id, status (ok, warn or error) and message.

Examples:
  doctor
  doctor {"offline": true}
